from connected_research_case import ResearchAuthor,present_case

a=ResearchAuthor('ai-7/32')
if 'Two 45-minute sessions.' in str(a.w):a.replace_text('Two 45-minute sessions.','Use the three-session teaching cycle above, with extra time as needed.')
present_case(a,
 headline='Respond to review with traceable evidence and concrete corrections',
 purpose='Address the concern, preserve original records and distinguish proposed analysis from completed evidence.',
 intro='A reviewer’s concern asks whether the evidence supports the claim. A response should connect that concern to a specific record, correction or justified scope change. Calling a neural network advanced does not answer a request for a baseline comparison. If the needed evidence is absent, either propose a clearly identified new analysis or narrow the existing claim. Do not write that a test was completed when it has only been suggested.',
 contract=[['Review item','Complete supplied exercise contract'],['Main concern','Fitted-line baseline comparison is missing'],['Main response','Neural network is advanced, without comparison results'],['Evidence status','No new baseline counts, design or raw outcomes supplied'],['Main repair options','Fair comparison under an explicit plan, labelled new analysis; or narrower claim'],['Separate picture','Four views of P1 plus four views of P2'],['Underlying source identities','Eight photos, two plants; not eight independent plants'],['Review artifact','Concern, response, change location, evidence and status'],['Limits','No actual reviewer communication, new experiment or source-independence proof']],
 ledger=[['Main response step','Evidence-grounded alternative'],['Identify concern','Does performance differ from a fitted-line baseline under aligned conditions?'],['Reject unsupported defense','Advanced architecture is not comparative evidence'],['If no comparison exists','Narrow the claim to the actual recorded comparison'],['If new comparison is proposed','Specify aligned cases/metric/eligibility and label new analysis'],['Change location','Identify the actual manuscript section/artifact when revised; do not invent it'],['Status','Proposed, completed or blocked, with corresponding evidence'],['Preserve history','Original claim, response and later analysis remain distinguishable']],
 picture='The separate picture has four views of plant P1 and four of P2, so eight photos represent two distinct plant IDs. A claim of eight independent plants is unsupported. Changing the word photos to plants does not change the source structure. Revisit the sampling/inference unit, group allocation across data roles and any uncertainty calculation that assumed eight independent plant observations. The picture supplies no correctness labels or split assignment, so neither a revised accuracy nor actual leakage can be inferred. Correct grouping does not create more plants, and two different IDs do not prove independent sampling.',
 picture_table=[['Source grouping','Photo views','Plant identities'],['P1','V1, V2, V3, V4','One'],['P2','V1, V2, V3, V4','One'],['Total','Eight photos','Two distinct plant IDs'],['Unsupported analysis premise','Eight independent plants','Source structure contradicts this count'],['Required reconsideration','Grouping, split roles and uncertainty assumptions','Not just a word replacement'],['Outcome/split evidence','Not supplied','No invented revised score or known leakage']],
 probes=[['Review-response audit','Checked interpretation'],['Reviewer asks for baseline','Answer with a comparison or a narrower claim'],['Author says advanced','Architecture praise is not evidence'],['New analysis planned','Keep status proposed until artifacts/results exist'],['Eight photos from two plants','Do not count eight independent plants'],['Correct the word only','Does not repair downstream unit assumptions'],['Two plant IDs','Not proof of independent sampling'],['Missing failure counts','Provide actual counts/denominators or disclose absence'],['Delete limitation paragraph','Hides concern rather than resolving it']],
 investigation='Create a paper response record for the missing baseline: concern, supplied evidence, proposed response, proposed change location and status. State that no new baseline experiment is supplied. Then count picture photos and plants and list the analysis assumptions needing review, without inventing outcomes or split leakage. Any manuscript location is a proposed destination until an actual edit exists. Preserve original and revised reasoning. This exercise sends no message and performs no model run. Reserve the independent missing-failure-count response for its first attempt.',
 teacher_key='Main advanced-network wording does not answer the baseline request. Require a fair documented comparison labelled new work, or a narrower claim using actual evidence; do not fabricate results. Picture has eight photos but only two plant IDs: four views each. Revisit grouping, role allocation and uncertainty assumptions that treated views as independent plants. Word replacement alone fails. No revised outcome rate or actual split leakage is supplied. Independent response should report actual failure counts with denominators, locations and evidence, preserve relevant limitations and disclose any missing records. Deleting limitations does not answer the concern. No actual communication, completed experiment or independence guarantee occurs.',
 reference='Peer review tests evidence, methods and clarity. For each comment record concern, response, change location, evidence and status. Main reviewer requests a fitted-line baseline, while the author only calls a neural network advanced. That supplies no comparison. Add an explicitly planned fair comparison and label it new analysis, or narrow the claim to existing evidence. Proposed tests are not completed results. Separate picture has four views of P1 and four of P2: eight photos from two plants. Eight independent-plant observations are unsupported. Revisit grouping, data-role allocation and uncertainty assumptions, not merely wording. Different IDs do not establish sampling independence, and no labels/split assignments are supplied for a revised rate or actual leakage diagnosis. Correct grouping cannot create more evidence. Missing failure counts need real records/denominators or an honest statement of absence, not deletion of limitations. This is a fictional paper response exercise, not a message to a reviewer.',
 independent='Explain how an evidence-backed response should handle missing failure counts while retaining limitations.',
 image={'type':'image','src':'/api/resource/ai-7-32-review-units','alt':'Plant P1 has four photo views, and plant P2 has four. Eight photos represent two distinct plant identities, not eight independent plants. Review grouping, data roles and uncertainty assumptions; changing wording alone does not repair the analysis. No outcome labels or split assignments are supplied.','caption':'Source-unit correction in a fictional reviewer concern. Correct counting does not prove independent sampling or create additional plants.'})
